30,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Oh no! Our software partners are totally swamped with board seats, but the logistics experts are just sitting there. Also, finding shift supervisors takes forever!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,George,,"My findings are telling. Our wins came from quiet back-office tools, while the write-off involved physical premises. However, independent practices and field instruments have great retention.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,May,,"This is worrying. Follow-on calls for equipment are way higher than we planned, and our credit line is useless for subscription-based security. We're leaking cash.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Rin,,I found out that anything with hardware or depots adds six weeks and a huge fee to our audits! But at least hardware lets us verify figures independently.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"It's just as I feared. Security reviews for medical or financial data take three times longer, and hardware shortages have caused massive delays in the past.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@May, that sounds scary! Does that mean we can't pick something that needs a lot of money?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,George,,"@Mizuki, if hardware causes such delays, perhaps the high retention George mentioned isn't worth the operational headache.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,May,,"@Mio, exactly. We need to be very careful. If we back something with heavy equipment, we might not have the reserves to sustain it.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Rin, wait, I mean @May! If hardware makes the audit a nightmare, maybe we should avoid it entirely to save our sanity at quarter-end.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, the data is clear. The ""hidden"" obstacles are usually physical supply chains or heavy regulatory reviews. We need a path with fewer hurdles.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Mio,,"But if we avoid hardware, we have all these logistics advisers who aren't doing anything! That feels like a waste.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,George,,"@Mio, it is better to have an idle adviser than a failed company. The evidence shows back-office software is where our actual success lies.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,May,,"I agree with George. Between the credit line restrictions and the follow-on call rates, a lean software model is the only way to protect our liquidity.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Rin,,And it would make the reporting so much easier! No more outside appraisals and six-week delays.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"We are seeing a pattern. Hardware brings verification and retention, but it also brings delays, audit costs, and funding drains.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Mio,,I guess I can handle the partners being busy if it means we don't go broke!,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,George,,"It seems we are aligning on a preference for low-overhead, software-driven solutions.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,May,,Precisely. Stability and solvency must come first.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Rin,,I'm totally on board with anything that makes the last fortnight of the quarter less miserable!,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"Then we are looking for a candidate that is lean, avoids heavy regulation, and doesn't rely on physical supply chains.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
