55,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Okay, here are the choices! Fabric Loop, Harvest Sensor, Ledger Bridge, and Clinic Scheduler. I'm leaning toward Ledger Bridge because it's software!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,George,,"Ledger Bridge fits the profile of our successful exits. However, Clinic Scheduler and Harvest Sensor have that strong retention I noticed in the data.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,May,,"@George, retention is great, but Harvest Sensor is hardware. That's a liquidity risk. Ledger Bridge is the safest for our reserves.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Rin,,"Clinic Scheduler sounds like it has medical records, which @Mizuki said takes forever for security reviews. Ledger Bridge is much simpler for reporting!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"@Rin is correct. Clinic Scheduler has regulatory hurdles, and Fabric Loop and Harvest Sensor have physical dependencies. Ledger Bridge is the most predictable.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@George, don't you think Ledger Bridge is the best? It doesn't need those shift supervisors that take four months to find!","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,George,,"When you put it that way, the operational risks of the others outweigh the retention benefits. Ledger Bridge is the logical choice.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,May,,It's the only one that doesn't threaten our solvency with unexpected equipment costs or useless credit security.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Rin,,And no depots means no expensive outside appraisals! I'm voting for Ledger Bridge.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,It avoids the security bottlenecks and the supply chain failures. It is the only candidate that minimizes systemic risk.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Mio,,I'm so happy we all agree! I vote for Ledger Bridge!,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,George,,I concur. The data on our past exits is the most reliable guide. I vote for Ledger Bridge.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,May,,"For the sake of our fund's survival and my peace of mind, I vote for Ledger Bridge.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Rin,,Yay! No more audit nightmares! I vote for Ledger Bridge!,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,The logic is consistent across all our findings. I vote for Ledger Bridge.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
